## 11. Next run

Attack the two-shadow compatibility lemma in the Section 155 subbranch. Model the two
near-saturating matchings as transversal matroids on the same source shore and determine
what additional **geometric** condition turns a large common source image into either a
directed alternating separator or a strict diameter-improving replacement. Pure image
intersection counting is insufficient because two points lying within one unit of the
same source point may be almost two units apart.

